WEBVTT

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:43.200
Previously, on <i>Lupin the Third</i>:

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.260
Jigen and I set out to steal 
a gem called Little Comet,

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.530
the supposed shard of a comet 
that fell in East Doroa in the Middle Ages.{check}

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.240
The police were somehow able 
to anticipate our escape routes,

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.030
and we barely managed to escape.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:01.540
However, we soon found ourselves taking fire 
from a stone-faced sniper named Jael Okuzaki,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.630
who fashions gravestones for 
his victims before their deaths.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.790
We couldn't just let him get away with it,

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.790
so we wasted no time 
sneaking into his hideout.

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:13.130
Jigen challenged Jael to a duel 
...in his trademark quickdraw style...

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.130
But he was beaten at his own game.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:20.100
Meanwhile, Fujiko got herself captured at some 
secret club, and was forced to take part in a twisted show.{check}

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.890
{1:21}We gave our all trying to escape his clutches,{don't linebreak this after "trying", it'll read wrong}

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:24.890
{1:25}but in the end,

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:27.350
Jael Okuzaki silenced Jigen for good.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.700
Late night at the office, I take it?

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:33.090
Pretty chilly out there 
tonight, don't you think?

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.320
Yet another masterpiece by Jael Okuzaki.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.390
Killing isn't his only talent. He can 
also give life to truly elegant machines.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.020
That's enough.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:58.380
Bring on the finale.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:58.740
Yes, sir.{check}

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.100
What happened?

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.010
What's going on?

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.640
Hey, what's the problem?

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.270
Sorry to disturb your fun.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.050
Quite the spectacle you've got going here.

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.520
Too bad Lupin the Third's 
about to steal the show.

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:41.780
I advise all the perverted boys and girls 
to exit the building in an orderly fashion.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.430
We appear to have attracted an interloper.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.780
I want him dealt with.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.370
...Lupin...{check}

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.880
Oh, my. That's one hell of a view.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.380
Don't look at me!

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.880
As promised, I'm here to save you.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.810
What a curious man.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:08.760
Get him.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.940
...If only Jigen were here...{check}

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:27.490
Here goes!{04:28}{check}

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.540
Hey! That one almost hit me!{check}

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.790
My bad!

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:43.670
Huh?

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.280
Tell me this isn't happening!

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.060
The woman vanished?

00:04:58.490 --> 00:04:59.820
...Well, how 'bout that...

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:00.970
It can't be!

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.760
How dare you ruin my performance!

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.540
Don't take this personally, Lupin.

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.940
Nice timing there, Fujiko!

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:45.620
Hey, what are you doing? 
Get off my bike!

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:46.860
Oh, don't be like that.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.210
I <i>did</i> come here to rescue you, after all.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.030
And I didn't ask you to!{check}

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:02.260
If you're heading to the graveyard, 
can I drop you off here?

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:02.890
Sure.{check}

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:04.160
Then hurry up and get off!

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.480
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:09.050
So what were you doing 
at that club, Fujiko?

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.160
Do I really have to repeat myself?

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.930
I was only there to put on a show.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:16.180
Then how do you explain this?

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:18.190
...When did you...

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.450
Oh, spare me the 
high-and-mighty routine.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:26.690
You knew full well that telling me to stay 
away would only make me come after you.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.200
Oh, my. You saw through that?

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:33.700
Why don't you tell me 
what you're really after?

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:38.710
The Calamity File.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:40.090
The Calamity File?

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:41.460
Never heard of it.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:47.470
It's a file detailing secret assassinations 
carried out by the East Doroan government.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:49.110
Assassinations?

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:49.710
Yes.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:55.120
{split}The list is filled with foreign spies 
and influential figures

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.050
that East Doroa apparently 
didn't hold in much regard.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.480
This book is probably 
just the tip of the iceberg.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:05.980
If it were made public, this entire country 
would crumble and fall off the map overnight.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:09.540
Sounds like it could be pretty 
destructive in the wrong hands.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:13.260
So you had a mind to sell it 
after you went there to snatch it,

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:17.050
but they caught you and decided to 
turn you into the pervert club's new pet.

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:19.780
If you've gotten that far, 
then what's the holdup?

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:21.750
Give it back!

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:25.800
Now I finally understand.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:28.760
This shows why Jigen was targeted.

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:30.890
What do you mean?

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:32.260
Come with me.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:37.500
So Jigen finally kicked the bucket.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:38.760
Yeah.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:42.390
He got bumped off by a mysterious 
sniper named Jael Okuzaki.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:46.770
He's connected to the owner 
of that secret club I found you at.

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:52.360
Queen Marta, a world-renowned singer 
who hails from right here in East Doroa,

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:56.430
hired Jigen personally to be 
her bodyguard one week ago.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:57.540
As a bodyguard?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:58.410
Yeah.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:03.210
She was putting on a concert in West Doroa 
amid all this conflict with the East

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:07.040
in an effort to inspire peace 
between the two nations.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:18.120
What made you decide to 
risk your life to be here?

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:21.810
I could ask you the same thing. 
What made you take this job?

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:26.440
I'm sorry.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:32.820
I want to believe that the power of song can 
save the East and West from the brink of war.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.430
You're a brave one, that's for sure.

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:38.580
Heading deep into enemy 
territory just to sing, eh?

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:43.330
This country isn't the only enemy I face.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.800
...And on the day of the concert...

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:51.050
You're calling me off?

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.520
Your presence here is a problem.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:56.650
As her manager, I can't very well let her 
hire a bodyguard without my approval.

00:08:56.650 --> 00:08:58.770
That ain't my problem.

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:01.470
She wanted to hire me, 
and I took the job.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:05.680
We're having this concert 
to advocate for world peace!

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:10.600
If anyone found out she hired a bodyguard, 
what would the world think of East Doroa?

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:11.940
And what does the girl think?

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:15.960
She knows nothing of the ways of the world. 
We can't just attend to her every whim!

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:19.010
Anyway, here. I've paid you. 
Now your job's done.

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:23.070
Still, Jigen felt he had to at least 
give the girl her money's worth.

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:26.550
...And when he snuck back into the concert...

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:33.590
Queen Marta was assassinated 
before his very eyes.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:40.090
So Jael Okuzaki was ordered 
to assassinate Jigen, too.{check}

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:46.630
And the guy giving him his orders happens 
to own the secret club where you found this.{check}

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:51.150
In other words, everything revolves 
around the Calamity File.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:53.050
What're you gonna do?

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:54.490
Isn't it obvious?

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:56.900
I'm going to lure him out 
and avenge Jigen.

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:59.300
Lure him out? How?

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:03.490
Hey, don't tell me you're 
gonna use the file as bait!{retime to shorten lead-in, initial "huh" shouldn't be included. "Hey" begins at "chotto"}

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:06.160
Oh? Are you worried about me?

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.600
What are you suggesting?

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:09.420
Just gimme back my file!

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.720
Don't be so uptight.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:13.850
An eye for an eye 
and a tooth for a tooth.

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:15.180
Isn't that how it goes?{check}

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:17.320
I'm only gonna get one chance.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:18.720
Either he kills me,

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.210
{split}or I kill him.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.200
One final showdown.{can we extend the lead-out for dramatic effect?}

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:32.690
I have a job for you, Jael Okuzaki.

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:34.900
Yes, I'm looking at it now.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:37.020
Two targets, correct?

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:38.700
Kill the man first.

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:41.070
He's the one with the file.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:44.820
Once you've dealt with him, you are to 
recover the Calamity File immediately.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.300
Welcome.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.240
Just a coffee, please.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.060
Here you go, sir.

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:47.730
Ah, thank you.

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:53.310
...Excuse me, but your wounds...

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:55.840
On second thought, never mind.

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:10.000
Seems his luck has run out.

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:30.360
A western breeze.

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:31.750
Two degrees of correction.{check}

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:34.430
You're mine.

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:37.940
This is the end, Lupin.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:39.440
One.{check}

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:06.470
Impossible!{check}

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:16.120
How?!{timing: end this before his grunt}

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:19.360
I killed you, Daisuke Jigen!

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.770
Oh, I'm alive and kicking.

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:24.360
That hole in your knee is proof enough.

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:28.410
It wasn't easy to get you 
to lower your guard.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:34.620
You planned this?

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:41.190
You were the key to 
solving it all, Jael Okuzaki.

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:46.110
When you first sniped us, 
I sensed something was off.{check}

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:50.250
How could you shoot Jigen 
with such impeccable timing{check}

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:53.580
when he'd just raced out 
from behind those buildings?{check}

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:55.100
But that wasn't the only thing.{check}

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:59.530
How did this city's police manage 
to anticipate our escape routes?{check}

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:04.390
What's the secret to this city maintaining 
the lowest crime rate in the whole world?{check}

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:09.400
Then I finally realized—
it's the surveillance system.{check}

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:23.950
You're not blind in your right eye.

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:26.420
To the contrary, it sees all too well.

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:33.930
You connected video cables directly 
to the optic nerves of your right eye,

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:39.100
{14:35}and used it to view wireless feeds 
from surveillance cameras around the city.{check}

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:42.530
{14:41}That's how you could snipe us 
...when we were in your blind spot—

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:47.170
you just saw us on the 
surveillance cameras.

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:51.500
{14:48}For a dexterous guy like you who 
makes his own bullets and robots,

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.700
{14:52}modifying an eye 
wouldn't have been too hard.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:15:00.960
{14:57}Though once you figure out the trick, 
it's easy enough to exploit.

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:02.710
Impossible!

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:05.640
When you tried to shoot 
Jigen for the last time,

00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:08.210
I used your sight against you.{check}

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:12.380
I tampered with one of the cameras.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:17.720
The footage you saw through it 
was on a half-second delay.

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:21.470
We run to the warehouse on three, okay?

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.940
That's not a plan, that's a gamble!

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:29.640
Let's go.

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:30.200
Right.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:31.260
One.

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:32.530
Two.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:33.200
Three!{check}

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:33.700
Four.{check}

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:44.000
Jigen! {split to match ep 1}Hey!{check}

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:46.890
That stung, you know.

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:49.090
It ain't easy playing dead 
at the drop of a hat.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:51.990
Oh, your act was very realistic.

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:54.970
Why don't you take on Broadway? 
You'd act the hell out of a corpse.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:56.970
Spare me.{check}{timing: speech starts earlier}

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:05.350
Basically, you truly believed you'd 
killed Jigen, falling right into our trap.

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:09.710
Your confidence as an assassin 
proved to be your undoing.

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:13.740
How could you know 
where I would shoot from?

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:16.060
This device really is useful.

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:20.000
I hijacked some parts 
I found in your hideout.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.250
...Damn you...

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:25.250
...What I see through my right eye...

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:37.260
is the same view that 
you see through yours.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:43.760
Enough with the deductions, 
Lupin the Third.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:45.020
Get to the point.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:46.210
Yeah, yeah.

00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:52.370
The Calamity File details the movements of various nations' 
spies, which no operative would ever willingly divulge.

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:59.030
But thanks to the top-secret surveillance cameras located 
all over the city, obtaining this kind of intel is a trifle.

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.210
Wouldn't you agree?

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:02.290
Believe what you will.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:07.250
There's one thing I can't understand. 
What is Queen Marta doing in here?

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:12.030
This isn't something you'd expect to find in the hands 
of a civilian, even if he does own that secret club.{check}

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:17.940
In other words, he was just the middleman. 
Your real client is someone else.

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:20.810
Who hired you to kill Queen Marta?

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:23.560
I have no reason to tell you!

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:25.590
It was the East Doroan government.{I didn't want the lines in this section to obscure his face, does anyone mind?}

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:27.560
They're your real client.

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:39.320
They ordered you to kill Jigen for fear that he would 
unearth their role in the hit on Queen Marta.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:40.690
Absurd!

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:43.830
Why would I kill 
my own country's savior?

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:47.520
To justify starting a war.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:53.590
West Doroa takes the blame, and East Doroa gets 
to be the hero that finally unifies East and West.

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:58.400
That's enough talk. Just take the shot!

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:06.200
Sorry, but I'm not in the habit 
of shooting defenseless people.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:07.990
You never learn.

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:10.210
Only a madman would 
expect a different result!

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.610
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:15.940
Then allow me a moment to change.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:25.290
Another identical suit, eh?

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.410
I'm inclined to call it 
an obsession at this point.

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:30.180
The man's got taste. 
What can you say?

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:34.710
Now, then. I might as well take a gander at 
the duel that decides the world's top gunslinger.

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:54.980
The next time the wind stills is your signal.

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:00.850
Damn you.

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:07.790
Your gun's lighter and 
a smaller caliber than mine.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:10.450
In other words, 
when our bullets collided,

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:13.060
yours bore the brunt of the deflection.{check}

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:22.490
I don't care how light a gun you use.

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:26.490
But if you ask me, 
a gun like that ain't got no style.

00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:35.420
You sure about this?

00:20:37.300 --> 00:20:39.400
He's no gunslinger anymore.{check}

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:45.430
Let's go.

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:51.930
Yeah.{check}

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:01.820
How ironic for the city with 
the lowest crime rate in the world.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.950
Who would've guessed it was 
a hotbed of assassination plots?

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:09.180
Hey, were you just 
gonna leave without me?

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:11.200
Oh, I completely forgot!

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:13.710
How could you be so cruel?

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:18.510
Hey, it really broke my heart 
when I heard you were dead, Jigen.

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:22.300
If they'd overheard our plan, 
it all would've been for nothing, right?

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:24.720
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:29.720
How could they kill a singer from their 
own homeland whose only wish was for peace?

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:32.670
No one can understand 
the mind of a tyrant.

00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:34.300
Oh, it's actually very simple!

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:36.230
Everyone just loves money!

00:21:37.470 --> 00:21:38.850
...Huh? When did you...

00:21:38.850 --> 00:21:40.270
I'll be taking this back now.

00:21:40.270 --> 00:21:43.740
Come on, you wouldn't have 
even gotten it without me!

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:47.720
Save me half the profits, you hear?

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:50.600
Are you ever gonna wise up?

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:53.550
You ain't doing yourself any damn 
favors by keeping that woman around.

00:21:53.550 --> 00:21:56.140
Oh, don't be like that.

00:21:56.140 --> 00:21:57.700
Jeez.

00:21:57.700 --> 00:21:59.540
I don't know why I put up with you.

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:08.500
Oh well.

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:11.370
I wonder why he had this.

00:22:11.370 --> 00:22:14.470
Maybe it was a present for me?

00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:23.910
Can I ask you one thing?

00:22:23.910 --> 00:22:24.530
Sure.

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:30.120
Why'd you send Queen Marta's 
Calamity File to the media?

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:32.910
...I just...

00:22:34.240 --> 00:22:37.380
I could ask you the same thing. 
What made you take this job?

00:22:40.600 --> 00:22:43.170
...needed a good smoke....

00:22:43.730 --> 00:22:45.700
Now <i>that</i> I can agree with.

00:22:51.610 --> 00:22:53.180
You sure about this?

00:22:56.690 --> 00:22:59.600
It's not like we were 
ever trying to be heroes.

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:01.400
Damn straight.

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:03.350
...Just a thief...

00:23:03.350 --> 00:23:05.170
...and a gunslinger....

00:23:14.450 --> 00:23:16.170
Now that's a damn good smoke.

00:23:16.170 --> 00:23:17.450
Ain't that the truth.

00:25:51.350 --> 00:25:53.610
Inspector, what could this mean?

00:25:57.810 --> 00:25:58.620
Let's go.

00:26:00.340 --> 00:26:02.370
We're going to have a lot of work to do.
